editorial implicit modules are selected by the dead-export census: true
select arms use the compiled target interface relationship: true
public generator inputs follow Dune module ownership and explicit interfaces: true
parser tokens and lexer body changes produce generated-interface review entries: true
private generated modules of a public library remain conservative entries: true
Dune empty-interface policy changes produce publication-input review entries: true
availability preprocessing and driver inputs remain literal review evidence: true
independent public configuration field reordering stays quiet: true
independent Dune stanza reordering does not create API drift: true
Dune module ownership moves produce conservative publication-input entries: true
owning generator configuration changes produce manual-review entries: true
independent generator configuration field reordering stays quiet: true
select configuration is visible when its target has an implicit interface: true
select configuration with an explicit target interface stays quiet: true
private generator configuration edits remain manual-review entries: true
private ownership dependency and prose edits do not change publication entries: true
module lists and configuration read from other files refuse: true
a bare include atom, a variable named like a read pform and an include outside module owners and generators pass: true
a selected interface target refuses by name: true
re-exported dependencies remain publication-input evidence at any depth: true
ordinary dependency edits beside a re-export stay quiet: true
ordinary private modules remain in the census inventory: true
a multiline value signature change is visible: true
record fields and constructors retain their symbol spellings: true
documentation and whitespace changes do not count as declarations: true
floating and nested documentation attributes do not count as declarations: true
floating implementation documentation is discarded recursively: true
nested signatures and includes stay in the checklist: true
implicit lets externals and types including deriving changes are visible: true
non-documentation attribute payload changes stay visible: true
unnamed initializers anonymous modules and bare evaluations do not count as exported declarations: true
named pattern aliases remain exported declarations: true
named module unpack bindings remain exported declarations: true
extension inputs stay visible even when their payload binds no source name: true
non-documentation attributes on anonymous items refuse with their location: true
named items and extension payloads keep their attributes without refusal: true
anonymous bindings inside mixed let groups do not create drift: true
pattern extension inputs remain visible without an ordinary binder: true
declaration movement across opens is visible in signatures and implementations: true
adding a declaration does not report every following unchanged declaration: true
declaration removals and additions are distinct: true
invalid OCaml refuses instead of reporting an empty inventory: true
compact rendering keeps both headers, the changed lines, context and omitted counts: true
distant edits are separate hunks and near ones share context: true
full rendering prints both sides; one-sided entries print in full when compact: true
a moved but unchanged entry says only its position changed: true
line edit scripts reconstruct both sides, beyond the comparison bound too: true
